<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Himmatnagar</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ahmednagar (Gujarat)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Himmatnagar is a town in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, headquarters of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabarkantha-district">Sabarkantha district</a>, on the Hathmati river. Founded in the 15th century as Ahmednagar by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-shah-i-of-gujarat">Ahmad Shah I of Gujarat</a>, it became the capital of Idar State and was renamed after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> Himmat Singh in the 20th century. It is now a regional commercial centre.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/himmatnagar.jpg" alt="Himmatnagar" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Viral A Dave · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Himatnagar_Public_Library_and_Towerclock.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
